Running Sugarscape Experiments on Bridges-2

# Project Goal

This project investigates how different interest rates affect agent behavior in Sugarscape, including wealth distribution, inequality, population growth, lifespan, and loan activity.

Environment
Platform: PSC Bridges-2
Project Allocation: cis260191p
Python Version: Python 3

# Configuration

Simulation configuration files are generated automatically using:

make configs

This creates a set of experiment configurations in the configs/ directory. The experiments compare the following lending conditions:

baseline_no_lending
standard_lending
low_interest
high_interest
low_lending_factor
high_lending_factor
short_duration
long_duration

Each condition is generated with 10 randomized runs using different seeds, resulting in a total of 80 configuration files.

# Running Experiments

Experiments are submitted to Bridges-2 through Slurm using:

make submit-array

This launches an array job where each interest rate configuration is executed 10 times with randomized seeds, for a total of 60 simulation runs.

Job status can be monitored with:

squeue -u

All simulation outputs are saved in the results/ directory, and Slurm log files are saved in the logs/ directory.